{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794622062,"nonce":"5jiT7OStjK20G1G6ZdvWg+i+iS4=","title":"Licences as a table, with versions","message":"The reader links every CC BY and CC BY-NC text to the 4.0 licence, but 31 of the 40 Storybooks Poland stories (PR #71) are under 3.0 (20 CC BY 3.0, 11 CC BY-NC 3.0). CC 3.0 4(a) needs the URI of that licence.\n\nPlan: a licence table like tag (id, name, url, shareable), with versioned ids (cc-by-3.0, cc-by-4.0, …); document.licence a foreign key to it instead of the CHECK from migration 0005; existing values renamed to their 4.0 ids; GET /api/licences for the upload form and credit links; the public-needs-shareable rule from the shareable column. Then set the 3.0 stories' files to their versions.\n\nAlso from the same attribution review:\n- Liczymy zwierzęta fixes a typo in the source (\"to wodopoju\" -\u003e \"do wodopoju\"), so it's a modified copy, which BY 4.0 3(a)(1)(B) says to indicate. Revert it or say so.\n- The Storybooks author lines don't name the African Storybook original; its source page does. Could add it: \"…; translated by Aleksandra Migorska from African Storybook's \u003ctitle\u003e\".\n- Wolne Lektury's reuse rules ask online reuse to name Wolne Lektury; the credit's link just says \"source\". Showing the source's name or domain would cover it.","files":null}]}